        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marrowstone%2C_Washington",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Nordland General Store, Marrowstone's only grocery, reopened in 2024 as a community‑owned co‑op after a 2020 fire.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marrowstone%2C_Washington",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Every Memorial Day weekend, island residents parade tractors in front of the Nordland General Store.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marrowstone%2C_Washington",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A narrow causeway once linked Marrowstone to Indian Island; it was removed and replaced by a low bridge in 2022‑23 to restore salmon passage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        12,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marrowstone%2C_Washington",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The island’s post office, called Nordland, has operated since 1898 for over a century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marrowstone%2C_Washington",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Marrowstone overlooks Port Townsend Bay and Admiralty Inlet, the entrance to Puget Sound.",
